course: dictionary
lesson: 12066
title: The clavicle, or collarbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A clavicle is the long, thin bone that joins the top of your breastbone to your shoulder. Its other name is the collarbone. You have one on each side. Context helps you find its meaning: «The X-ray showed that his clavicle was cracked after the fall.» A fall, an X-ray and a cracked bone all point to a bone that can break.
explain: Feel for it yourself. «Touch the bone at the top of your chest, then slide your fingers out along the clavicle to your shoulder.» Your fingers follow a thin bone that curves across the top of your chest. That is the clavicle, and it sits near the front of your shoulder.
explain: Sport and safety lessons often mention it. When a cyclist falls and lands on an outstretched arm, the force can travel up the arm into the shoulder, and the clavicle may snap. «Every person has two clavicles, one on each side.» So if one breaks, the other is still there to help you tell which side is hurt.
fact: Clavicle is another name for the collarbone.
fact: A clavicle is a long, thin bone between the breastbone and the shoulder.
fact: You have two clavicles, one on each side of your body.
fact: A clavicle can break after a fall onto an outstretched arm, for example from a bike or a horse.
exercise: «The X-ray showed a cracked clavicle.» What is a clavicle? | A type of cloud | A muscle in the stomach | *The collarbone, a long thin bone near the shoulder | A tooth at the back of the mouth
exercise: Where is the clavicle? | *Between the top of the breastbone and the shoulder | In the foot | Down the back of the leg | Inside the skull
exercise: How many clavicles does a person have? | Four | Three | One, in the middle of the chest | *Two, one on each side
test: Dan fell off his horse and landed on his outstretched arm. The doctor said his clavicle was broken. Which part of Dan's body is hurt? | His knee | *His collarbone | His wrist | His ear
test: Which word is another name for the collarbone? | Patella | *Clavicle | Radius | Femur
exam: Which sentence uses the word clavicle correctly? | The clavicle is the sound a bell makes | The clavicle is a type of fruit | *The clavicle is the long, thin bone between the breastbone and the shoulder | The clavicle is the colour of the sky
